# Component Patterns

## MANDATORY: Check Existing Components First

**Before creating ANY component, check:**

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Error display | `ErrorMessageDialog` |
| Confirmation | `QuestionConfirmationDialog` |
| Custom modal | `BaseDialog` |
| Toast | `NotificationSnackbar` |
| Tag input | `CreatableTagSelector` |
| Dropdown | `DropDownSelector` |
| Text input | `InputField` |
| Data table | `TableGrid` |

Locations:
- `components/common/dialogs/`
- `components/inputs/`
- `components/common/`

## Component Structure

```typescript
import { useState, useCallback, useMemo } from 'react';
import { useTranslations } from 'next-intl';

interface Props {
  id: number;
  onUpdate?: (data: any) => void;
}

const Component: React.FC<Props> = ({ id, onUpdate }) => {
  const t = useTranslations('namespace');
  // ...
};

export default Component;
```

## Key Rules

- ✅ Always define TypeScript interfaces for props
- ✅ Use `useTranslations` for all user-facing text
- ✅ Use `useCallback` for event handlers
- ✅ Use `useMemo` for expensive calculations
- ✅ Include loading and error states
- ✅ Use semicolons at end of statements
- ❌ Don't create new components if existing ones work
